// twinspeak.rc -- v6.6.4: app icon + version info. v7.5.3..v7.7.9: version
// bumps (the full per-version notes live in CHANGELOG.txt).
// v8.0.0: THE KERNEL LOOP + REALTIME. Both legs open WDM-KS pins by default
// (the kernel-level loop: twinspeak's own AvrtPriorityCritical thread writes
// each bite the instant the DAC's position register says the lead was
// consumed -- no events, no scheduler; wasapi exclusive is the automatic
// fallback and the opt-out). One-time ini migration carries pre-8.0.0
// templates over. The engine takes REALTIME_PRIORITY_CLASS (HIGH fallback,
// logged). The pump spin-pacer's danger zone follows the transport. Version
// steps to 8.0.0.
// v7.8.1: THE CAPTION PING -- the theme click landed
// DWMWA_USE_IMMERSIVE_DARK_MODE but Windows 10's DWM repaints its caption
// only on a render-state CHANGE, so the titlebar stayed stale until
// minimize/restore; guiApplyDwmMode now pings WM_NCACTIVATE(FALSE)/
// WM_NCACTIVATE(TRUE) after the attribute set and the flip lands in the
// same click. (Details in twinspeak.cpp's changelog.) Version steps to
// 7.8.1.
// v7.8.3: DROP CORRECTION -- the ring restarts instead of crackling. A deep
// underrun (>= half the buffer switch is hole) silence-fills, holds the leg
// while the pump rebuilds the ring to its target anchor, then skips the
// silent gap oldest-first and resumes at the freshest capture with the
// original latency. New ini key drop_correct (default on; GUI pill on the
// SETTINGS page), logged as 'drop corr', counted in the devbuf line.
// Version steps to 7.8.3.
// v7.9.0: THE SPIN PACER. The v6.1 line had demoted the MAINS pump from
// TIME_CRITICAL (31) to HIGHEST (10) -- at 100% CPU the mains pump starved.
// Both pumps stay time-critical now and rank INSIDE MMCSS (center =
// AvrtPriorityCritical, mains = AvrtPriorityNormal). New pump spin pacer:
// when an out ring falls under 2 device periods + 1 capture burst of
// headroom the pump busy-waits with _mm_pause for a bounded 1.5 ms and
// drains the instant capture lands. KS pacers spin through the last period
// + 0.5 ms of slack against the DAC's position register. New device-switch
// lateness meter logs "the DAC grazed the buffer edge" -- evidence for any
// residual device-side static. The banner prints the real TWS_VERSION (the
// old v7.1.19 literal is gone).
// Version steps to 7.9.0.
// v7.8.4: THE SHALLOW-STAIRCASE FIX + THE CENTER FADE. A SUSTAINED run of
// shallow shortfalls (7 of the last 16 switches short -- the ring hovering
// just above empty at 100% CPU) now escalates to the same clean restart a
// deep shortfall gets; an isolated shallow miss still replays in place
// (sample-continuous, inaudible). The center upmix guard engages after 2
// consecutive fingerprint hits, releases after 8 consecutive misses, and
// fades ch3 over 2.5 ms instead of hard-zeroing at a block boundary. The
// drop_correct ini key and GUI pill are gone (integrated, always on).
// Version steps to 7.8.4.
// v7.8.0: THE ONE-FILE WINDOW HEADER RETIRES, WHOLE -- no include, no stub
// file, no external chrome API. The window is the flat default Windows 10
// frame (a stock WS_OVERLAPPEDWINDOW: native caption, icon, title, min/max/
// close, sysmenu, resize, shadow), and every dark theme re-dials
// DWMWA_USE_IMMERSIVE_DARK_MODE from the theme's background lightness so
// the native titlebar follows the app's dark/light themes (attribute 20
// with the 19 fallback, re-applied on every applyTheme and at creation).
// The DPI child ledger lives in twinspeak.cpp now. Version steps to 7.8.0.
// (the historical v7.5.x..v7.7.x window work -- the one-file window
// header's arrival and every uDWM byte-chase it bought -- is retired with
// it; the notes are preserved in CHANGELOG.txt)
// No windows.h include needed -- the VERSIONINFO and
// RT_MANIFEST forms used here are RC syntax, not C macros, so both windres
// and zig rc accept this file as-is.
// v7.1.20: `1 24` embeds twinspeak.manifest (RT_MANIFEST = 24, id 1) --
// DPI awareness (the blur fix), comctl32 v6 (DarkMode_Explorer), asInvoker.
// v7.1.21: the manifest's XML comments lost their "--" (illegal inside XML
// comments -- the SxS loader refused the whole file and the exe would not
// start: "side-by-side configuration is incorrect").
1 ICON "twinspeak.ico"
1 24 "twinspeak.manifest"

1 VERSIONINFO
FILEVERSION     8,0,0,0
PRODUCTVERSION  8,0,0,0
FILEOS          0x40004L
FILETYPE        0x1L
FILESUBTYPE     0x0L
BEGIN
    BLOCK "StringFileInfo"
    BEGIN
        BLOCK "040904B0"
        BEGIN
            VALUE "CompanyName",      "TidyVision"
            VALUE "FileDescription",  "TwinSpeak Control Panel"
            VALUE "FileVersion",      "8.0.0.0"
            VALUE "InternalName",     "twinspeak"
            VALUE "LegalCopyright",   "Copyright 2026-beyond TidyVision -- MIT License"
            VALUE "OriginalFilename", "twinspeak.exe"
            VALUE "ProductName",      "TidyVision TwinSpeak"
            VALUE "ProductVersion",   "8.0.0.0"
        END
    END
    BLOCK "VarFileInfo"
    BEGIN
        VALUE "Translation", 0x409, 0x4B0
    END
END
